[{"id":3824398362,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7j87Aa","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?u=af70f5d107e9c1447f296643d5a566dab53d25e8&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116456#pullrequestreview-3824398362","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116456","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116456#pullrequestreview-3824398362"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116456"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-19T15:26:54Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3836032309,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7kpTU1","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"For the visualization, I would prefer having more polygons on the sphere, maybe try 16 / 16 ring count instead of 8 /8 . Right now it's really blocky and that makes it distracting or even confusing to look at the constraint because the edges look like a part of the constrained area.\n\nAlso, it is important to show 0 angle tracks/segments in the constraint. in the meeting iFire said there is some disabled line drawing code, which would be fine. But if that's too difficult to get working, I would be okay with maybe *in the gizmo only*, clamp a minimum angle like 1 degree and draw that for tracks less than 1 degree and that should illustrate to users that it is moving along this track.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116456#pullrequestreview-3836032309","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116456","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116456#pullrequestreview-3836032309"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116456"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-21T21:08:03Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3870831667,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7muDQz","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?u=9b90963f1b4f17720e50bbbe495fbe8c84c8bc8e&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"As a serious issue, results become unstable when there are three or more holes.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4b49b92d-b03c-4c44-8407-278d8b7cb853\n\nBased on testing, the result is stable with two holes.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8f1fe8bc-aae9-4e0a-9580-eeadab058f6e\n\n[kusudama_test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25640319/kusudama_test.zip)\n\nTherefore, if we implement this in 4.7, we should consider statically limiting the number of holes to two. If we statically limit holes to two, two structures come to mind.\n\n---\n\nOne is the same as the current implementation and just having two holes internally:\n\n```cpp\nstruct HoleSetting {\n  Vector3 direction;\n  real_t radius;\n}\n\nHoleSetting begin_hole;\nHoleSetting end_hole;\n```\n\n---\n\nThe other approach is to eliminate the Vector specification and instead treat it as a arc-shaped area spreading in the ±Z directions, with the offset delegated to JointLimitation:\n\n```cpp\nreal_t arc_angle; // 0 to 360deg. How to spread start and end to +Z and -Z. for example, 180deg means start hole dir is Vector3(0, 0, -1) and end hole dir is Vector3(0, 0, 1).\nreal_t start_radius; // -Z\nreal_t end_radius; // +Z\n```\n\n<img width=\"272\" height=\"215\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9967c752-213a-486d-b5c6-3fb403172cc7\" />\n\nOffset is set by:\n<img width=\"443\" height=\"226\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/692bf65d-c666-4e59-9b3d-a21690fd60ac\" />\n\nThe reason it expands in the Z direction is because HumanoidProfile defines X rotation as a Bend.\n\nIn other words, specifying individual vectors makes sense when there are three or more holes. However, when there are only two holes, specifying individual vectors is redundant with the rotation offset parameter. This means the hole direction can be automatically generated from the arc parameter without necessarily specifying it individually.\n\n---\n\nPersonally, I think the latter approach makes the role of the offset clearer and allows for more intuitive range manipulation.\n\nIf we don't plan to abandon implementing the three holes in the future (after 4.7), I think providing the two static hole approach as a class called JointLimitationArc is a somewhat good compromise. How do you think?","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116456#pullrequestreview-3870831667","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116456","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116456#pullrequestreview-3870831667"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116456"}},"submitted_at":"2026-02-28T21:58:08Z","commit_id":null},{"id":3949373463,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7rZqgX","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?u=c2e06a3d2b49a467aa907e54aa259516440267cc&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","followi